{"book":{"id":"book-restoration-the-fall-of-napoleon-in-the-course-of-european-art-1812-1820-thomas-crow","slug":"restoration-the-fall-of-napoleon-in-the-course-of-european-art-1812-1820-thomas-crow","title":"Restoration: The Fall of Napoleon in the Course of European Art, 1812-1820","authors":[{"id":"person-thomas-crow","name":"Thomas Crow"}],"isbn13":["9780691253046"],"subjects":["Biography"],"topics":["Climate, Weather & Disaster","Art, Music & Performance","Empire & Colonialism","Essays & Cultural Criticism"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Restoration%3A%20The%20Fall%20of%20Napoleon%20in%20the%20Course%20of%20European%20Art%2C%201812-1820%20Thomas%20Crow","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Restoration%3A%20The%20Fall%20of%20Napoleon%20in%20the%20Course%20of%20European%20Art%2C%201812-1820%20Thomas%20Crow","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Restoration%3A%20The%20Fall%20of%20Napoleon%20in%20the%20Course%20of%20European%20Art%2C%201812-1820%20Thomas%20Crow","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Restoration%3A%20The%20Fall%20of%20Napoleon%20in%20the%20Course%20of%20European%20Art%2C%201812-1820%20Thomas%20Crow","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20186914W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-laura-shannon-european-studies-laura-shannon-prize-2020-official-shortlist","source-open-library-restoration-the-fall-of-napoleon-in-the-course-of-european-art-1812-1820-thomas-crow","source-cover-open-library-restoration-the-fall-of-napoleon-in-the-course-of-european-art-1812-1820-thomas-crow","source-open-library-summary-restoration-the-fall-of-napoleon-in-the-course-of-european-art-1812-1820-thomas-crow"],"publicationYear":2018,"thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-restoration-the-fall-of-napoleon-in-the-course-of-european-art-1812-1820-thomas-crow.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"essayistic","score":1,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"essay\"","catalog text contains \"essays\"","catalog text contains \"criticism\"","literature/criticism subject or topic"]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":28,"criticalRenown":67,"controversy":8,"llmAffinity":73,"affinityResidual":-1.11,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.85,"criticalRenown":0.82,"controversy":0.75,"llmAffinity":0.86},"tags":{"craft":"structural-invention","evidence":"close-reading","stance":"revisionism"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"summary":"As the French Empire collapsed between 1812 and 1815, artists throughout Europe were left uncertain and adrift. The final abdication of Emperor Napoleon, clearing the way for a restored monarchy, profoundly unsettled prevailing national, religious, and social boundaries. In 'Restoration', Thomas Crow combines a sweeping view of European art centers-Rome, Paris, London, Madrid, Brussels, and Vienna-with a close-up look at pivotal and significant artists, including Antonio Canova, Jacques-Louis David, Theodore Gericault, Francisco Goya, Jean-Auguste-Dominique Ingres, Thomas Lawrence, and forgotten but meteoric painters Francois-Joseph Navez and Antoine Jean-Baptiste Thomas. Whether directly or indirectly, all became linked in a new international network in which changing artistic priorities and possibilities emerged from the ruins of the old. Crow examines how artists of this period faced dramatic circumstances, from political condemnation and difficult diplomatic missions to a catastrophic episode of climate change. Navigating ever-changing pressures, they invented creative ways of incorporating critical events and significant individuals into fresh artistic works.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Art, european","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-restoration-the-fall-of-napoleon-in-the-course-of-european-art-1812-1820-t